course: dictionary
lesson: 12747
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A duct is a tube or pipe that carries something from one place to another. «The air duct carried warm air into every room.» You can picture a tube running along a wall or under a floor, carrying the air.
explain: Ducts can be in buildings or inside your body. «Her tear duct carried tears from her eye down to her cheek.» Here duct means a small tube in the body. The words around duct tell you which kind it is, so read the whole sentence.
explain: Duct also appears in «duct tape», which is not a tube at all. «Dad fixed the torn tent with duct tape.» Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence? If it does not, look at the other words for clues.
fact: Duct means a pipe or tube that carries things such as air, water or cables.
fact: «Air duct» means a tube in a building that carries heating or air conditioning.
fact: «Tear duct» means a small tube in the body that carries tears.
fact: «Duct tape» means very strong sticky cloth tape.
exercise: «The air duct carried warm air into every room.» What does duct mean here? | A loud noise | *A tube that carries air | A kind of cake | A pet mouse
exercise: «Mum put a strip of duct tape over the hole in the tent.» What is duct tape? | A soft blanket | *Very strong sticky cloth tape | A thin paper for drawing | A kind of rope
exercise: Where would you find a tear duct? | In your big toe | In your ear | In your elbow | *Near your eye
test: «Cables ran through a duct under the floor.» What does duct mean here? | A hole in the ground for water | *A tube that carries cables inside a building | A door made of wood | A toy car
test: Which phrase means a tube in a building that carries heating or air conditioning? | *Air duct | Air fan | Duct tape | Tear duct
exam: «He crawled through the air duct to reach the secret room.» What is the air duct in this sentence? | A kind of cave | A road for cars | A pet mouse | *A tube in a building that carries air
